# Valgrind suppressions for apteryx-rest test runs.
#
# apteryx-rest runs its FastCGI handlers on a GLib thread pool and lets GLib
# spawn a helper thread for UNIX signal handling. GLib does not join every one
# of those threads before the process exits, so the per-thread stack/TLS that
# glibc allocates in pthread_create() is still owned by the thread when valgrind
# takes its snapshot. Valgrind reports it as "possibly lost", and occasionally
# (depending on the exact teardown interleaving) as "definitely lost" - a 0-byte
# block. None of this is an apteryx-rest heap leak; it is thread-lifecycle noise
# from GLib, so suppress the per-thread TLS allocation regardless of leak kind.
#
# Scope is deliberately tight: only the dynamic linker's thread-local storage
# allocated by pthread_create() is matched (apteryx-rest never allocates heap
# through that path). Regenerate/extend with valgrind --gen-suppressions=all.

{
   glib-pthread-tls-stack
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite,possible
   fun:calloc
   fun:calloc
   fun:allocate_dtv
   fun:_dl_allocate_tls
   fun:allocate_stack
   fun:pthread_create@@*
   ...
}
